{(\textbf{Generalized Adjustment Criterion (GAC)})}
   Let $\g$ represent a $\mathrm{DAG}$, $\mathrm{CPDAG}$, $\mathrm{MAG}$ or $\mathrm{PAG}$. Then $\mathbf{Z}$ satisfies the generalized adjustment criterion
      relative to $(\mathbf{X,Y})$ in $\g$ if the following three conditions hold:
   \begin{itemize}
   \item[(0)] $\g$ is adjustment amenable relative to ($\mathbf{X,Y}$), and
   \item[(1)] no element in $\mathbf{Z}$ is a possible descendant in $\g$ of any $W \in \vars\setminus\mathbf{X}$ which lies on a proper possibly causal path from $\mathbf{X}$ to $\mathbf{Y}$, and
   \item[(2)] all proper definite status non-causal paths in $\g$ from $\mathbf{X}$ to $\mathbf{Y}$ are blocked by $\mathbf{Z}$.
   \end{itemize}

